From: "Codebuff Agent (via dhaupin)" <noreply@codebuff.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 20:28:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix LSB carrier: reader was dead on arrival; adopt Vant's
 canonical [len][packet] wire
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The LSB path could never work: lsbRead called _b2B (bits→bytes),
which was never defined — every onload threw inside the promise, so
LSB decode hung forever. And even with that fixed, the reader expected
an 8-byte SGF binary header (0x534746 magic + version + length) that
lsbWrite never emitted (it wrote a bare packet, no framing at all).
Writer and reader never agreed on anything.

This PR:

- Defines _barr2b (the missing _b2B), and replaces the SGF framing
  with the canonical wire Vant's PNG pipeline emits as of pass 178:
  [4-byte big-endian payload length][packet bytes], MSB-first, one
  bit per pixel in the R channel's LSB, x-major.
- Rewrites _lsbExtract as a single, testable packet parser with the
  "BRN:" (colon INCLUDED) start-of-packet guard, so random noise
  images correctly read as no-payload rather than garbage-packet.
- Sizing: lsbWrite now dims for header + packet (the old writer
  sized for packet alone — it never accounted for a header because
  it never wrote one).
- Drops legacy SGF read branches from _up (writer never emitted SGF)
  and from the test copy of _up which had drifted from index.html.
- Tests: 5 new wire-level tests (round-trip long/short, noise plane
  null, non-BRN packet empty, exact Vant-layout pin) — suite 25/25.
- README + AGENTS LSB sections now describe the real wire; new
  docs/lsb-spec.md pins the cross-system contract (also fixes an SVG
  extraction snippet that referenced a data-p= attribute no code
  writes).

Cross-decode verified against dhaupin/vant branch axolotl (pass-178
stego rework): Stegoframe wire parses a Vant stone, and Vant extracts
a Stegoframe wire — both directions OK.

